    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d815">

                <pb facs="0921" n="809" xml:id="pg809"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.52/346</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Consul General at Canton</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Spiker</hi>)<anchor n="44" xml:id="d815-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-18T14:00:00+08:00">April 18, 1935—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Legation perceives no objection to American property holders voluntarily
                    registering title deeds in the manner described in your despatch No. 17, April
                    4, provided no restrictions are placed on their treaty rights to acquire, and
                    dispose of, leases in perpetuity at Canton. Legation desires you to obtain as
                    soon as possible and forward by air mail with your comments copy of Chinese text
                    and English translation of deed form to be issued under the new procedure.</p>
                <p>British Legation states it is prepared to acquiesce in proposed re-registration
                    at the same time reiterating its position that valid title deeds must be
                    recognized and insisting upon the right of British subjects freely to transfer
                    title deeds.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d815-f1" n="44" type="source" xml:id="d815-f1-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted to the Department by the Minister in China in his despatch No.
                    3526, April 20; received May 18.</p>
            </note>
